      "name": "swarm-monitor",
      "title": "Supervising active swarms, maintaining cold-start handover continuity, and translating worker state for humans",
      "description": "Supervises any active multi-agent swarm bound to a parent Swarm Work Item (`epic` or `milestone` in `beans`) on event-driven wakeups and a 2-to-4-minute fallback timer: maintains measurable exit criteria (`EC-1..EC-k`), structured child queues (`completed`, `active`, `queued`, `idle-backlog`), and a live Cold-Start Handover Runbook pushed to `cat/cat-harness/beans` on every routine check-in; checks CPU, disk, and compressed/swap memory headroom; keeps compute-bound workers productive on non-heavy `idle-backlog` work; hands verified pull requests to the merge steward; and publishes standardized two-table human status reports (`on-demand` or `periodic`) free of internal session shorthands.",
